<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <%= render 'layouts/header_mail' %>
  <body>
    <h4>Dear <%= @user.name %>,</h4>
    <% if @notifications > 0  %>
        You have <%= pluralize(@notifications, "new notification") %>. <%= link_to "Log in", @url_login, class:'mail-btn'  %> to see your unread <%= "notification".pluralize(@notifications) %>!
    <% end %>
    <p>
      smartXchange will be hosting its first event ever! This Friday, January 27, we will host an event from 18.00-20.00 at the European Institute for Entrepreneurship, C. General Arrando 9, Madrid, Spain.
      If you are in Madrid and would like to meet other people from smartXchange and Madrid, pay €4 and register for the <a href="https://www.eventbrite.es/e/entradas-smartxchange-networking-event-31420940880">smartXchange networking event</a>
      or pay €5 at the door.
    </p>
    <p>
      We hope you are sticking to your new years resolutions!
      smartXchange is proud to have entered its seventh month since launching, and we hope you are brushing up on your Spanish/English/German/Italian/French before Valentines day! Learning a phrase or two of your partner's language is the most romantic gift to give :).
      Over the past month we have expanded to over 200 users and are in talks with forming our first partnership.
      We have also greatly improved our user search functionality and added a much requested feature, the Xchange option.
      It is now easier to search for people to practice or exchange languages with, with search by language and language level (i.e. 'English a1 a2 lawyer') or by nationality (i.e. 'Spanish tutor') or both nationality and language (i.e. 'USA Spanish developer a1 a2') or by keywords (i.e. 'developer').
      To use the new Xchange option, click the Xchange link (on the People page) and smartXchange will show you your best language exchange options, localized and matched according to your language level and interests.
    </p>
  </body>
  <%= render 'layouts/footer_mail' %>
</html>
